parser blind spot (the real question):
- TASK_RE still MISSES (probed directly, not guessed): `**A / B —**`,
  `**A, B —**`, `**A and B —**`, `**H1**` (bold, no title dash), and
  heading style `### **H1 — …**` / `### H1 — …`.
- Worse than a miss: a dual-ID header is not dropped, it is ABSORBED. A doc of
  `H1` + `**H2 / H3 —**` + `**H4, H5 —**` parses as ONE task (H1) and
  check() returns ok=True, 0 errors, 0 warnings — the two blocks and their
  fields silently fold into H1's body. So a whole task can hide behind a green
  gate, which is exactly how M8.D1/D2 vanished.
- worktree_audit.py propagates it (imports todo_check.parse_tasks).
  progress_report.py has its own bounded `^- \[.] \*\*<id>` regex: it reports
  `task not found` for a requested ID rather than absorbing — a visible bug,
  not a silent one, but the same ID-shape hole.
- Current board: 176 `- [ ] **`-shaped lines vs 175 parsed; the 176th is the
  fenced field template at line 176 (correct). 175 is luck, not a guard.

